# QuickTextFormatter environment template
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# No environment variables are required to run this frontend locally:
#   npm run dev
#   npm run build
#   npm start
#
# Keep real .env files out of Git. Any variable beginning with NEXT_PUBLIC_
# is embedded into the browser bundle, so it must never contain a password,
# private token, or other secret.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public site URL (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used while building canonical URLs, hreflang links, Open Graph URLs,
# sitemap.xml, and robots.txt. Use the public production origin only (no path).
#
# Where to get it:
# - Use the HTTPS URL configured for the production domain in your hosting
#   provider (currently https://www.quicktextformatter.com).
# - This is not a credential and does not require an API key.
#
# If omitted, the code falls back to https://www.quicktextformatter.com.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.quicktextformatter.com

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Analytics 4 measurement ID (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by components/GoogleAnalytics.jsx to load the site's GA4 web tag.
# A measurement ID is public configuration, not a password or secret.
#
# Where to get it:
# 1. Sign in to the Google Analytics property that owns this website.
# 2. Open Admin > Data collection and modification > Data streams.
# 3. Select the Web data stream and copy its Measurement ID (G-XXXXXXXXXX).
#
# Current application behavior:
# - If this is empty, the app uses its built-in site ID: G-Q0M38E72DJ.
# - The current code only accepts that built-in site ID; a different ID is
#   ignored until components/GoogleAnalytics.jsx is intentionally changed.
# - Do not put a Google password, service-account JSON, or private API key here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel deployment context (normally supplied automatically; do not set)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel provides this during builds and runtime as production, preview, or
# development. The project uses it to no-index preview/non-production builds
# and to generate a disallow-all preview robots.txt.
#
# Where to get it:
# - It comes automatically from Vercel when the project is deployed there.
# - It is not a credential and should not be copied from a GitHub token.
#
# Leave unset locally unless you are deliberately testing preview behavior.
# VERCEL_ENV=development

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials checklist
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project currently has no required database, auth, payment, email,
# storage, server API, or private third-party credentials. Text conversion and
# analytics calculations run in the browser, and Vercel Analytics does not
# require a project token in this repository.
#
# The GitHub personal access token used to publish the repository is a Git
# credential, not an application environment variable. Never add it here.
